From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guruswamy Basavaiah <guruswamy.basavaiah@broadcom.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kpatch: match __cfi_/__pfx_ stubs tolerant of function padding

With CONFIG_CFI_CLANG=y and Photon's gcc-rap-plugin-with-kcfi.patch, the
compiler emits a __cfi_<func> (or __pfx_<func>) stub at the start of each
function's .text.<func> section, followed by CONFIG_FUNCTION_PADDING bytes,
then the function itself. Example (meminfo.o):

    __cfi_meminfo_proc_show : st_value=0x0  st_size=5
    meminfo_proc_show       : st_value=0x10 (=16)   (same section)

kpatch_link_prefixed_functions() matched the function only at the exact
offset (stub st_value + st_size). Because the stub size (5) does not include
the 11-byte function padding, the function at offset 16 is never found and
the build aborts with "missing func for __cfi_<func>", even for the patched,
indirectly-called function whose type-id must be preserved.

Match by the nearest following STT_FUNC in the same section instead of an
exact offset. This is padding-agnostic and still resolves the no-padding
case (offset == stub_end). Aliases (multiple functions at the same offset)
are all linked, as before. If no following function exists, a __cfi_ stub
for an __init function (.init.text, discarded after boot, never livepatched)
is skipped; anything else remains a hard error.

Signed-off-by: Guruswamy Basavaiah <guruswamy.basavaiah@broadcom.com>
---
--- a/kpatch-build/kpatch-elf.c
+++ b/kpatch-build/kpatch-elf.c
@@ -453,12 +453,15 @@
 static void kpatch_link_prefixed_functions(struct kpatch_elf *kelf)
 {
 	struct symbol *func, *pfx;
-	bool found;
 
 	if (kelf->arch != X86_64)
 		return;
 
 	list_for_each_entry(pfx, &kelf->symbols, list) {
+		bool found = false;
+		unsigned long best_value = 0;
+		struct symbol *base;
+
 		if (!pfx->name || pfx->type != STT_FUNC)
 			continue;
 
@@ -466,25 +469,68 @@
 		    strncmp(pfx->name, "__cfi_", 6))
 			continue;
 
-		found = false;
-
+		/*
+		 * Find the function this prefix stub belongs to: the nearest
+		 * STT_FUNC in the same section that starts at or after the end
+		 * of the stub. An exact "stub_end" offset is not reliable -
+		 * with CONFIG_CFI_CLANG / Photon's gcc-rap-plugin-with-kcfi the
+		 * function is placed after the stub plus CONFIG_FUNCTION_PADDING
+		 * bytes, so the __cfi_ stub's size does not reach the function.
+		 * Matching by "closest following function" is padding-agnostic
+		 * and still works for the no-padding case (offset == stub_end).
+		 */
 		list_for_each_entry(func, &kelf->symbols, list) {
-			if (func->type == STT_FUNC && func->sec == pfx->sec &&
-			    func->sym.st_value == pfx->sym.st_value + pfx->sym.st_size) {
-
-				/*
-				 * If a func has aliases, it's possible for
-				 * multiple functions to have the same 'pfx'.
-				 */
-
-				pfx->is_pfx = true;
-				func->pfx = pfx;
+			if (func == pfx || func->type != STT_FUNC ||
+			    func->sec != pfx->sec || !func->name)
+				continue;
+			/* skip other prefix stubs (e.g. a __pfx_/__cfi_ pair) */
+			if (!strncmp(func->name, "__pfx_", 6) ||
+			    !strncmp(func->name, "__cfi_", 6))
+				continue;
+			if (func->sym.st_value <
+			    pfx->sym.st_value + pfx->sym.st_size)
+				continue;
+			if (!found || func->sym.st_value < best_value) {
+				best_value = func->sym.st_value;
 				found = true;
 			}
 		}
 
-		if (!found)
-			ERROR("missing func for %s", pfx->name);
+		if (found) {
+			/*
+			 * Link every function at that closest offset; aliases
+			 * share the same prefix stub.
+			 */
+			pfx->is_pfx = true;
+			list_for_each_entry(func, &kelf->symbols, list) {
+				if (func == pfx || func->type != STT_FUNC ||
+				    func->sec != pfx->sec || !func->name)
+					continue;
+				if (!strncmp(func->name, "__pfx_", 6) ||
+				    !strncmp(func->name, "__cfi_", 6))
+					continue;
+				if (func->sym.st_value == best_value)
+					func->pfx = pfx;
+			}
+			continue;
+		}
+
+		/*
+		 * No following function at all. A __cfi_ stub for an __init
+		 * function (.init.text, discarded after boot, never livepatched)
+		 * can be safely ignored; anything else is a genuine build error.
+		 */
+		base = NULL;
+		if (!strncmp(pfx->name, "__cfi_", 6))
+			base = find_symbol_by_name(&kelf->symbols,
+						   pfx->name + 6);
+		if (base && base->sec &&
+		    !strncmp(base->sec->name, ".init.text", 10)) {
+			log_debug("skipping __cfi_ prefix for __init func: %s\n",
+				  pfx->name);
+			continue;
+		}
+		ERROR("missing func for %s", pfx->name);
 	}
 }
 
